@end
LANGUAGE FOCUS   "Marginal"
English marginal in economics and management accounting means at the margin — the effect of one more unit — and carries no suggestion of smallness or unimportance. In everyday English a marginal difference is a trivial one, and that reading destroys the technical sense completely: a marginal cost can be the largest number in a decision. Arabic حدي comes from حد, a boundary or limit, and keeps the technical meaning cleanly. French marginal has the same double life as English, with coût marginal technical and marginal in ordinary speech meaning peripheral — and French adds à la marge for the technical idea when clarity is needed. The exam uses the technical sense without exception.
